{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Split from silvern-dewy-damselfly (f4cf-60b2-41c0-4843). OPERATOR RULING (2026-08-21, latest\ncomment): option (a) approved — persist close provenance durably in the close STATUS event.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nAfter a close whose completion-signature append failed, a later reader cannot tell that\nticket apart from one closed with the gate off (damselfly reports the loss only in the\nreturned payload of the call that suffered it — ephemeral). The gate's state at close time\nis read from config and discarded (`_completion_precheck`, `_commands/close_precheck.py`),\nso \"closed with no attestation\" collapses into ONE state: gate off, `--force` close,\nconfig-unreadable fail-open, `source == \"local\"` unattested close, `certifiable is False`\nwithholding, and signature-append failure.\n\nPrerequisites, all landed:\n\n* steep-tired-whimbrel (f5c4-b2d1-4503-4bfe, CLOSED) — `gates.gate_enabled` now returns the\n  tri-state `GateState` (ENABLED / DISABLED / UNREADABLE); this plan CONSUMES that\n  tri-state, never recomputes it.\n* defiant-orthoclase-buck (055d-f176-8fcb-4ffe, CLOSED) — `force_close_reason` is now\n  persisted on the close STATUS event and folded; the discard this ticket originally\n  flagged is fixed. `force_bypassed` complements that durable reason.\n* Owner for `not_applicable` (operator decision): set explicitly on the `idea -> closed`\n  path in `transition_close.close_ticket`, the only place that knows the gate never applied.\n\n## Approach\n\nRecord on the `*->closed` STATUS event WHY a completion signature was or was not expected —\nin the SAME locked write that commits the close (`txn.transition_core`), so NO additional\nlock acquisition (an audit comment or second event would append through the very write-lock\nwhose timeout causes the failure being recorded, and be missing exactly when it matters).\n\n`completion_expectation` is a present-only string ENUM (a bool cannot separate the states\nthe ACs demand), total over the close path:\n\n| value | meaning at close time |\n|---|---|\n| `required` | the gate ran; a completion signature was expected |\n| `disposition` | a qualifying administrative close: signed as a DISPOSITION, not a completion PASS |\n| `gate_off` | a readable config had the gate off (GateState.DISABLED — a policy choice) |\n| `gate_unreadable` | unreadable config, gate failed OPEN (GateState.UNREADABLE — a FAULT, not laundered into `gate_off`) |\n| `force_bypassed` | `--force` skipped the gate (its reason is the sibling `force_close_reason`) |\n| `local_source` | verdict `source == \"local\"`: verified but never signed |\n| `not_certifiable` | `certifiable is False`: certification withheld (uncertified descendant) |\n| `not_applicable` | `idea -> closed`: a REJECT/DROP, not a completion |\n\nThe event records the EXPECTATION only, never the outcome — the STATUS commits BEFORE\nsigning is attempted. A reader combines it with the durable attestation: `required` +\nattestation = closed and signed; `required` + none = **signature LOST**; `disposition` +/-\nattestation = disposition-signed / disposition-signature-lost; anything else = not expected,\nand the value says exactly why.\n\nComputation and threading — NOT `verified_result` (None for force, gate-off, local and\nnot-certifiable alike, so it conflates the very states this separates):\n`_completion_precheck` already visits every branch and now returns the PAIR\n`(verified_result, completion_expectation)`; it is a private in-repo seam, and its direct\ncallers and monkeypatch sites in tests are updated to the pair in the same change.\n`close_ticket` sets `not_applicable` on the `idea -> closed` branch it already owns and\nthreads the value into `txn.transition_core`, which gains a keyword parameter and stamps it\npresent-only next to `close_class` / `force_close_reason` (their exact precedent).\nLifecycle-exempt types yield an empty expectation; their transition is refused before any\nevent is written.\n\nReduced state: `_fold_close_metadata` (`reducer/_processors_status.py`) folds it on the\nwinning `*->closed` edge under the same present-only + fork-winner-only rules as\n`close_class`; declared as a `$defs` enum in `schemas/common.schema.json`, referenced from\n`schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`, `types.py` regenerated (`python -m\nrebar.schemas.gen_types`). `rebar show` and the MCP `fetch_ticket` surface it with no\nfurther wiring (open dicts, `additionalProperties: true`).\n\nBackward compatibility (docs/event-schema.md + docs/migrations.md): additive, reducer-known,\npresent-only. A historical close event lacking the key reduces to state WITHOUT the key —\nabsent = unknown/legacy, never guessed. No migration; older readers ignore the additive key.\n\nComplexity budget: `transition_core` (15) and `_completion_precheck` (15) sit at the ratchet\nthreshold and `close_ticket` at its frozen ceiling (17), so the new logic lands via\nbehavior-preserving extraction along existing seams — the close-metadata stamping cluster\nout of `transition_core`, the gate-resolution/force head out of `_completion_precheck`, and\nif needed the plan-review close-gate block out of `close_ticket` — never a baseline bump.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` — return the expectation with the verdict; consume\n  the tri-state; extract the gate-resolution head helper\n* `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` — unpack the pair; `not_applicable` on\n  `idea -> closed`; thread into `transition_core`\n* `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py` — accept and stamp the field on the `*->closed` STATUS event\n  in the same locked write (extract the stamping cluster)\n* `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py` — fold on both `*->closed` edges\n* `src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json`, `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`,\n  `src/rebar/types.py` (regenerated) — declare the enum in reduced state\n* `docs/event-schema.md` — document the STATUS close-metadata fields incl. the new one\n* `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` (+ existing precheck/reducer test modules as their\n  contracts change) — the ACs below\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests (happy + failure/edge): one close per enum value read back from REDUCED state;\nthe three-way signed / signature-lost / gate-off separation; a single-lock assertion via a\ncounting monkeypatch on `txn._acquire_write_lock`; `gate_unreadable` distinct from\n`gate_off`; and the degrade path — a legacy close event with no key reduces to state with\nthe key ABSENT.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `completion_expectation` is written into the close STATUS event in the SAME locked\n      write as the close, taking no additional write-lock — verified by a test asserting the\n      lock is acquired exactly once during a close\n- [ ] A later reader, holding no lock and reading only reduced state, separates\n      closed-and-signed (`required` + attestation) from closed-with-signature-lost\n      (`required`, no attestation) from closed-with-gate-off (`gate_off`) — verified by a\n      test closing one ticket each way and asserting all three read back distinctly\n- [ ] Each of `force_bypassed`, `local_source` and `not_certifiable` is recorded as ITSELF\n      and never as `gate_off` — verified by a test per value\n- [ ] An unreadable config records `gate_unreadable`, never `gate_off` (a fault is not\n      laundered into a policy choice) — verified by a test\n- [ ] A qualifying disposition close records `disposition`, distinct from `required` —\n      verified by a test\n- [ ] `idea -> closed` records `not_applicable` (a REJECT/DROP is not a completion) —\n      verified by a test\n- [ ] The expectation is computed independently of `verified_result`, so a `--force` close\n      records `force_bypassed`, not gate-off — verified by a test\n- [ ] The field is documented in `docs/event-schema.md` and is present-only and\n      backward-compatible: a historical close event lacking it reduces to state with the key\n      ABSENT (unknown/legacy, never guessed) — verified by a test replaying a legacy close\n      event"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787353201131814001,"uuid":"d5306f6a-efdf-433c-901e-25d35720603c"}